      "dom_id": "question-53555",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226670/assets/a4ff0f0f932cf6f2c98f474e2d0d6d6450e5c6072608a4f2fab4cd50aa650d94.png)\n\nA circular plot of land has a diameter of $20\\,\\text{m}.$ What length of fence is needed to border this plot of land?",
      "worked_solution": "The length of the fence needed to border the circular land is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C=\\pi d,$ where $d=20\\,\\text{m}$ is the diameter.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC=\\pi \\cdot 20=20\\pi \\,\\text{m}.\n$$",
